@startuml
title StockPilot - Sequence Diagram: Financial Analyst

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

actor "Financial Analyst" as Analyst
participant "React UI" as UI
participant "API Client\n(axios)" as API
participant "FastAPI\nRouter" as Router
participant "Auth\n(JWT / RBAC)" as Auth
participant "Analysis\nService" as Analysis
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Yahoo Finance" as YF
actor Administrator as Admin

note over Analyst
  An analyst inherits every investor
  capability (verdicts, portfolio,
  journal). Only the strategy
  authoring and publishing flows
  are shown here.
end note

== 1. Create a strategy ==

Analyst -> UI : open Advisor, tune six factor weights
UI -> UI : validate weights total 100
Analyst -> UI : Save as Strategy (name)
UI -> API : POST /strategies {name, weights}
API -> Router : request + Bearer token
Router -> Auth : authenticate
Auth --> Router : authenticated analyst
Router -> DB : INSERT INTO strategies\n(owner_id = analyst, weights JSONB)
DB --> Router : created strategy
Router --> API : 201 Created
API --> UI : strategy appears in "My strategies"

== 2. Validate the strategy with a backtest ==

Analyst -> UI : Marketplace -> Request Publish -> Run Backtest
UI -> API : GET /analysis/{ticker}/backtest (strategy weights)
API -> Router : request
Router -> Analysis : run simulation
Analysis -> YF : fetch historical OHLCV
YF --> Analysis : price data
Analysis -> Analysis : composite signal per day
Analysis -> Analysis : simulate portfolio (vectorbt)
Analysis --> Router : trades, win rate, Sharpe,\ndrawdown, profit factor, return
Router --> API : 200 metrics
API --> UI : auto-fill the six metric fields
UI -> UI : evaluate each metric against thresholds
UI --> Analyst : per-threshold pass / fail checklist

== 3. Request publication ==

Analyst -> UI : Submit for Review (price)
UI -> API : POST /strategies/{id}/publish {metrics, price}
API -> Router : request
Router -> Auth : require_role(analyst, admin)

alt caller is an investor
    Auth --> API : 403 Insufficient permissions
    note right of Auth
      Blocked before any
      database access
    end note
else caller is analyst or admin
    Auth --> Router : authorised
    Router -> DB : SELECT strategy\nWHERE id = ? AND owner_id = me

    alt not found or not owned
        Router --> API : 404 Strategy not found
    else owned
        Router -> DB : SELECT platform_settings (thresholds)
        DB --> Router : live threshold values
        Router -> Router : re-validate all five metrics\n(server-side is authoritative)

        alt any threshold not met
            Router --> API : 400 with per-metric breakdown
            note right of Router : nothing is stored
        else all thresholds met
            Router -> DB : SELECT existing listing
            alt already in review
                Router --> API : 400 Already pending review
            else already verified
                Router --> API : 400 Already published
            else
                Router -> DB : INSERT / UPDATE listing\nSET status = 'review'
                DB --> Router : listing saved
                Router --> API : 200 {status: review}
            end
        end
    end
end
API --> UI : close dialog, refresh marketplace
UI --> Analyst : strategy shows "In Review"

== 4. Await administrator decision ==

Admin -> Router : POST /admin/listings/{id}/approve
Router -> DB : status = 'verified', listed_at = now(),\nstrategy.is_published = true
DB --> Router : updated
Router --> Admin : 200 verified

== 5. Track earnings on the Creator Dashboard ==

Analyst -> UI : open Dashboard
UI -> API : GET /strategies
API --> UI : strategies authored by this analyst
UI -> API : GET /marketplace
API --> UI : all listings
UI -> UI : match listings to own strategy ids
UI -> UI : earnings = SUM(price x sales_count)\nsales, ratings, published count
UI --> Analyst : earnings, sales, ratings,\nstatus of every authored strategy

@enduml
